===========================================================
   [  1455.] = [   1_455] = -1+x,y,z             
   [  1655.] = [   1_655] = 1+x,y,z              
                                                                                            "7022074   "  PLATON-H-BONDS   Page  422
====================================================================================================================================
   [  1665.] = [   1_665] = 1+x,1+y,z            
   [  2665.] = [   2_665] = 1-x,1-y,-z           
   [  2565.] = [   2_565] = -x,1-y,-z            
   [  1565.] = [   1_565] = x,1+y,z              
   [  1545.] = [   1_545] = x,-1+y,z             
   [  2666.] = [   2_666] = 1-x,1-y,1-z          

For C--H...Acceptor Interactions See: Th. Steiner, Cryst. Rev, (1996), 6, 1-57

H-Bond classification [G.A.Jeffrey, H.Maluszynska & J.Mitra., Int.J.Biol.Macromol.(1985),7,336-348]
------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
2-Centre   (linear)     D-H...X most prob. angle 160 deg  - also: G.A.Jeffrey & W.Saenger, Hydrogen Bonding in Biological Structures
3-Centre (bifurcated)   SUM of 3 angl. about H = 360 deg                    Springer-Verlag, Berlin, 1991, pp 20.
4-Centre (trifurcated)

